DaVinci Resolve Studio for Slackware Linux
==========================================

This SlackBuild packages the official DaVinci Resolve Studio installer into a
native Slackware (.txz) package.

Prerequisites & Source Download
-------------------------------
Download the official "DaVinci Resolve Studio <VERSION> for Linux" from:
https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/products/davinciresolve

Place DaVinci_Resolve_Studio_<VERSION>_Linux.zip in this directory or in
~/Downloads before running the SlackBuild.

GPU & Hardware Acceleration
---------------------------
DaVinci Resolve requires GPU compute capabilities for video processing:

1. NVIDIA GPUs:
   - Works immediately out-of-the-box with the official proprietary NVIDIA
     display driver (which includes the CUDA Driver API and NVENC/NVDEC).

2. AMD Radeon GPUs:
   - Requires OpenCL compute support. Install ROCm OpenCL runtime (rocm-opencl)
     or Mesa RustiCL OpenCL (with RUSTICL_ENABLE=radeonsi).
   - On legacy GCN AMD cards, run with: ROC_ENABLE_PRE_VEGA=1 davinci-resolve-studio

3. Intel Arc / Iris GPUs:
   - Requires Intel Compute Runtime (intel-compute-runtime / neo OpenCL).

Licensing
---------
DaVinci Resolve Studio requires a valid Blackmagic activation key or USB dongle.
License and application support directories in /var/BlackmagicDesign and
/opt/resolve/.license are pre-configured with full write access so regular
users can activate seamlessly.
